  "question": "A patient averages 5.5 hours of sleep. Her time in bed starts there and grows 15 minutes a week. How many weeks until 7 hours?",
  "value": 6,
  "unit": "weeks",
  "answer": "90 / 15 = 6 weeks.",
  "move": "A cure built from small steps is slow by design; plan for the wait.",
  "hint": "Turn the gap into minutes, then count the 15-minute steps.",
  "steps": [
    "Target minus start: 7 - 5.5 = 1.5 hours.",
    "1.5 hours = 90 minutes.",
    "90 / 15 = 6 weeks."
